          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12.  (i) Suppose ABCD is a parallelogram and M, N are midpoints of AB and CD respectively. Show that segments DM and BN trisect segment AC."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.167,
            0.881,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Use part (i) to find a procedure to trisect any given segment PQ. Find two other ways to trisect PQ, one using Exercise 11 above and a third using the Centroid Theorem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.405,
            0.238,
            0.628,
            0.331
          ],
